Pre-existing, unrelated regression-candidate observed during logs-first check of
customer/order/list and customer/order/running-orders (both endpoints under delta re-QA).

Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log carries a testing.ERROR [FAIL] line on every phpunit
Feature-test hit to these two endpoints:
  [2026-09-07 23:39:49] testing.ERROR: [FAIL] The resource owner or authorization server
  denied the request. {"type":"League\\OAuth2\\Server\\Exception\\OAuthServerException",
  "endpoint":"/api/v1/customer/order/list"}
(same shape for /api/v1/customer/order/running-orders)

Earliest occurrence 2026-09-07 23:39:49, which predates commit 534e53918 (cycle-1 fix,
2026-09-08 01:41:54) and even 5cc3fc64d (the original cycle-0 build checkpoint) --
this is present across the ticket's entire lifetime, not introduced by this delta.

Not a functional defect: every test hitting these endpoints (StoreDataFormattingNPlusOneTest
x6, this QA's own tinker-harness calls) still asserts/observes HTTP 200 with correct payload
data. Root cause is almost certainly Passport's AuthorizationValidator middleware attempting
real bearer-token introspection against the test harness's placeholder "Bearer test" header
before Passport::actingAs()'s guard override wins -- a test-only harness artifact, not a
production code path. Non-blocking, does not affect this ticket's verdict.
